<title>USA: Midwest Cash Grain PM- Higher futures prompt sales.</title>
<headline>Midwest Cash Grain PM- Higher futures prompt sales.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Higher CBOT corn and soybean futures Monday prompted an increase in corn and soybean sales by Midwest farmers, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Most of the sales were old-crop supplies, they said. Some basis bids were reduced in reaction to the increased sales.</p>
<p>The soft red winter wheat harvest slowly progressed.</p>
<p>Ohio dealers said about 70 percent of that state's crop was harvested with the later-cut grain having higher-than-preferred moisture. Test weights were down slightly from early-harvested fields, but dealers said the grain was of good quality and largely free of disease.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures, cash $/bu.</p>
